                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Despite the lack of music and some of the outdated visuals, Cloning Clyde still holds up as a true diamond in the rough.\n\nDefinitely one of the more unique puzzle platformers out there, switching between clones and transforming into different animals when the puzzle demands it always managed to stay unique and fresh as setpieces and level gimmicks began to combine themselves. This game is fun to just kick back, put on your own music, and think about how to get Clyde and his clones out of each situation.\n\nI'm not too big of a fan of the endgame, especially getting the 20 or so Clydes to all escape the level, but the beer gut physics, Clyde's sound effects, and the fact that Clyde screams like a blackbelt whenever you open up a can of whoop-ass more than makes up for it. I absolutely adore Cloning Clyde!",
